{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1169385-\u266a\u266b\u266a-dream-dream-dream-when-i-want-you-\u266a\u266b\u266a","id":1169385,"title":"\u266a\u266b\u266a Dream dream dream when I want you \u266a\u266b\u266a","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-21T09:40:00-08:00","id":1169385,"title":"\u266a\u266b\u266a Dream dream dream when I want you \u266a\u266b\u266a","content":"Obligatory music <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lX0ws6y7p5g\" data-code=\"lX0ws6y7p5g\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lX0ws6y7p5g/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> So I've got some trouble brewing for myself now. I have a player character whom's about to join a mystery cult that's about dream visions, Jungian psychoanalysis, and self improvment by getting to understand the dreams of oneself and how it get together in a larger Jungian (ergo astral realm) collective unconscious dream state. All this and dandy fine yes!<br /> <br /> But here's the catch, it's a human game (with crossover elements) and the cult in question are a part of a guardian labyrinth so they don't get the whole supernal picture, but they have some glimpses of occult truth and understanding. <br /> <br /> What I'm looking for, what and how can you use dreams in any meaningful and interesting way on it's own, preferably with rules and such.<br /> There doesn't seem to be much for normal mortals and dreams out there. Sure there is the Oneiros and the Temenos in deeper part of the Astral, but what about simple ol' dreams?<br /> Does it exist anything useful you can do while in the dreams that don't infringe to much on the Oneiros and Temenos for humans?<br /> <br /> As well, I have four dots worth of the Mystery Cult done and an idea that the fifth dot would be building something of an own realm inside the Temenos for the cult, something vaguely resembling an Emenation realm<br /> <br /> The Lucid ones<br /> * Get a specialty of Oneriomancy in the Occult skill<br /> ** Get a dot of the Library (occult) merit<br /> *** Gets 2 dots in the Dream merit (from mage 2ed)<br /> **** Gets the Astral Adept merit (from mage 2ed)<br /> <br /> So as you can see the leaders and guides of the cult gets some things actually done while sleeping, but what about the rest? Got some ideas or input? Maybe give 1 dot in Dream merit already to initiates even though that feels a bit OP<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T14:21:27-08:00","id":1169470,"title":"","content":"Changeling the Lost has always dealt heavily in dreams and dream manipulation. 2e has revised rules for fey oneiromancy, Dream Bastions (individuals dream), and Eidolons and props (dream actors and well... props). If you have manuscript available or have a friend who has funded the kickstarter the Dreaming Roads rules and Dream Infiltrator conditions could be useful for your Mystery Cult. Also wouldn't it be interesting for Labyrinth to redirect mortals from &quot;Supernal Truth&quot; to just to a form of fallen magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-21T15:17:20-08:00","id":1169494,"title":"","content":"I do have backed it and read through it, but I assume most of it just works for Changelings. Like normal lucid mortals can't really use dream shaping and so and such?<br /> Yeah i think that's kinda what the labyrinth is influencing the cult is doing. Kinda like &quot;the dream world is all there is, and all strangeness in the world is born from human archetypes&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://